      "description": "Watch Bayern München vs Stuttgart highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The Allianz Arena set the stage for a high-stakes Bundesliga clash as Bayern Munich hosted VfB Stuttgart on August 28, 2026. With 75,024 fans in attendance, the atmosphere was electric as both sides looked to secure a statement victory in the early stages of the campaign. Bayern Take the Initiative Bayern Munich established dominance early on, dictating the tempo through their midfield maestros. The pressure told in the 21st minute when Joshua Kimmich delivered a pin-point corner from the left. Dayot Upamecano timed his jump perfectly to power a header past the goalkeeper, giving the hosts a deserved lead. While Stuttgart attempted to claw their way back, with Grischa Prömel testing the defense, Bayern remained composed to head into the break with a narrow 1-0 advantage. A Dramatic Second-Half Turn The game exploded into life shortly after the restart. In the 52nd minute, Josha Vagnoman stunned the home crowd by volleying home an equalizer for VfB Stuttgart . However, the parity lasted just three minutes. Michael Olise restored Bayern 's lead with a clinical left-footed finish, once again assisted by the ever-reliable Kimmich . The momentum shifted entirely in favor of the hosts when Vagnoman 's afternoon took a turn for the worse, scoring an own goal in the 58th minute to make it 3-1. Closing Out a Convincing Win Despite having a goal ruled out by VAR for offside in the 64th minute, Bayern continued to pour forward. The introduction of fresh legs from the bench, including Ismael Saibari , proved decisive. In the 82nd minute, Aleksandar Pavlović tapped in from close range after a brilliant setup by Saibari and Olise . The rout was completed in stoppage time when Luis Díaz found the back of the net with a precise right-footed strike. The final whistle confirmed a dominant 5-1 victory for Bayern Munich , with Upamecano earning plaudits for a standout performance."
